      "key": "optimistic",
      "name": "Optimistic — Managed Transition",
      "label": "optimistic (managed transition)",
      "description": "Governments and corporations proactively invest in reskilling. New industries (AI safety, climate tech, care economy) absorb displaced workers. Historical analogy: Industrial Revolution with strong labor policy.",
      "color": "#00CC96",
      "narrative": "Under the **Optimistic** scenario, governments and large employers treat AI displacement as a known shock and act accordingly. Reskilling captures **50%** of at-risk jobs; new industries (AI safety, climate tech, the care economy) absorb displaced workers at **0.6% of the 2025 base annually**, starting in 2028.\n\nThe AI capability curve is also assumed to be slightly *delayed* (inflection +1 year vs. Base) because regulatory oversight modestly slows deployment in safety-critical sectors. Median unemployment peaks at **12.8% in 2027**, with the P75 band capped near **13.4%** and the P05–P95 envelope under **14.4%**. After the peak, the trajectory decays toward the new-industry absorption floor.\n\n**Historical analogy.** Closest match is the post-WWII labour reorganisation — large absolute disruption absorbed by deliberate institutional investment. This requires **political will at scale**, not technology alone.",
