      "description": "AI adoption outpaces any adaptation mechanism. Mythos-level capabilities generalize rapidly. Policy response is inadequate and delayed. UBI/safety nets arrive too late.",
      "color": "#AB63FA",
      "narrative": "Under the **Pessimistic** scenario, AI deployment outpaces every adaptation mechanism. The capability curve shifts **2 years earlier** (Mythos-level generalises faster than expected), reskilling captures only 2% of at-risk jobs, and new-job creation is essentially flat (~0.02% / yr starting only in 2035).\n\nMedian unemployment plateaus at **26.4% in 2030**, with a P25–P75 band of **24.9–27.7%** and a P05–P95 envelope of **22.9–29.3%**. The envelope barely contracts over the projection horizon: with reskilling and new-industry channels effectively closed, the labour market never reabsorbs the displaced supply, and UBI/safety-net debates arrive too late to matter.\n\n**This scenario is not a forecast.** It is a *failure mode*: the trajectory observed when the market is allowed to clear without intervention. Its value is calibrating how much the Optimistic policy interventions are worth.",
