      "description": "Claude Mythos (April 2026) triggers rapid capability generalization beyond cybersecurity. Software engineering, law, finance, and analysis face near-simultaneous disruption 2027–2029. Based on: SWE-bench 93.9%, autonomous zero-day discovery at scale.",
      "color": "#FFA15A",
      "narrative": "Under the **Mythos-Accelerated** scenario, the cybersecurity demonstration generalises. Mythos showed autonomous discovery of zero-days at scale — the model assumes that within ~12 months this capability propagates to law, finance, and adjacent analytical knowledge work.\n\nThe AI capability curve shifts **3 years earlier** (inflection ~2031), and the IT & Communications sector takes a +35 pp boost on direct-replacement fraction (vs. +10 pp in the Base Case). New-job creation is delayed to 2032 because the disruption hits white-collar professional roles that historically drove new industry formation.\n\nMedian unemployment reaches **26.3% as early as 2026** and holds near that level into the 2030s, peaking at **26.3% in 2031** with a P25–P75 band of **24.9–27.6%** and a P05–P95 envelope of **22.6–29.1%**. The peak level itself is similar to the Pessimistic plateau — the distinguishing feature is *timing*: the displacement arrives almost a decade earlier than the Base trajectory, leaving no window for slow-moving policy.",
